Joachim Trier and Eskil Vogt , the creative partnership behind 2026 International Feature Oscar Winner and nine-time nominee &#x201C;Sentimental Value,&#x201D; are set to receive the Nordic Honorary Dragon Award, the top honor at the G&#xF6;teborg Film Festival, the biggest film event in Scandinavia.

Norway&#x2019;s Trier and Vogt &#x2013; Trier directing, both writing &#x201C;Sentimental Value&#x201D; and their breakout &#x201C;The Worst Person in the World,&#x201D; starring Renate Reinsve &#x2013; join a star-studded lineup of prior Nordic Honorary Dragon Award recipients, such as Noomi Rapace (2026), Thomas Vinterberg (2025), Ruben &#xD6;stlund (2021), Stellan Skarsg&#xE5;rd (2020), Mads Mikkelsen (2019), Susanne Bier (2016) and Liv Ullmann (2015). blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Jennifer Lawrence Ranks Her Onscreen Kisses, Details 'New' Implants and Says Her 'Hunger Games' Bow and Arrow Was 'Stolen' in Andy Cohen Interview Australian Brothers Discover They Are Indian Cinema Royalty in WAVES Film Bazaar Documentary 'Dada & Us'

Trier and Vogt will pick up the award at G&#xF6;teborg&#x2019;s opening ceremony on January 29. One day later, they will deliver a Director&#x2019;s Talk at the Swedish city&#x2019;s Stora Teatern. G&#xF6;teborg will also screen a retrospective of the duo&#x2019;s films.

These began 20 years ago2006&#x2019;s &#x201C;Reprise,&#x201D; which began their Oslo Trilogy of &#x201C;Oslo, August 31st&#x201D; (2010), concluding with &#x201C;&#x201C;The Worst Person in the World&#x201D; (2021) which snagged Oscar nominations for Original Screenplay and International Feature Film.

&#x201C;Louder than Bombs&#x201D; (2015) marked their first English-language movie; &#x201C;Thelma&#x201D; picks up on the interplay between the supernatural, daily life and character&#x2019;s emotions which have feed Vogt&#x2019;s own hits as a director, &#x201C;Blind&#x201D; (2014) and &#x201C;The Innocents&#x201D; (2021).

Not coincidentally, the Award will be given at the 50th G&#xF6;teborg Film Festival, running next year over Jan. 29-Feb. 27, which is looking to from early signs to celebrate Nordic cinema and what it can bring to the table. Trier and Vogt&#x2019;s &#x201C;cinema of intimacy,&#x201D; as Trier once called, and the superb actors they work with to explore that is one case in point, stretching back to the films of Ingmar Bergman. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Described by Sweden&#x2019;s G&#xF6;teborg Film Festival as &#x2018;one of the most exciting creative partnerships in European cinema,&#x2019; Trier and Vogt have worked with some of Scandinavia&#x2019;s finest actors such as Stellan Skarsg&#xE5;rd and Renate Reinvse, both Academy Award nominated for &#x201C;Sentimental Value.&#x201D;

&#x201C;Joachim Trier and Eskil Vogt have a remarkable ability to portray people trying to understand themselves and find their place in the world,&#x201D; said Pia Lundberg, Artistic Director of G&#xF6;teborg Film Festival.

She added: &#x201C;With humor, melancholy and keen psychological insight, they explore life&#x2019;s biggest questions through seemingly small, everyday moments. It is a great pleasure to honour their shared body of work with this year&#x2019;s Nordic Honorary Dragon Award.&#x201D;

No Wicked, no Moana, no problem, because Lionsgate is saving the Thanksgiving week box office with The Hunger Games: Sunrise on the Reaping which is posting $21.25M in previews, the second best ever for the franchise behind 2013's Hunger Games: Catching Fire which lit $25.2M in its previews. It's also currently the second best previews YTD after Sony's Spider-Man: Brand New Day ($72M) and ahead of Universal's The Odyssey ($17.6M previews, $123.5M opening).

Other previews that Sunrise on the Reaping beat include Universal's Wicked from two years ($19.2M; $112.5M opening); for the longest time we heard that the latest feature take of a Suzanne Collins novel was outstripping the presales of that Ariana Grande and Cynthia Erivo female skewing musical. It's also ahead of Lionsgate's Michael ($12.6M previews, $97.2M opening) and light years ahead of the previous Hunger Games: Ballad of Songbirds and Snakes ($5.75M previews, $44.6M opening) which had its campaign impacted by the actors strike, not to mention the Collins novel about the origins of Coriolanus Snow wasn't a fan-fave. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories News Everything We Know About The 'Hunger Games: Sunrise On The Reaping' Movie So Far News 'Hunger Games: Sunrise On The Reaping' To Shine Brightly Around The World With $160M-$190M WW Debut - Box Office Preview

