SPOILER ALERT: This post spoils the end of The Hunger Games: Sunrise on the Reaping .

The epilogue scene at the end of The Hunger Games: Sunrise On The Reaping echoes the chapter that closes Suzanne Collins&#x2019; novel of the same name.

Woody Harrelson , Jennifer Lawrence and Josh Hutcherson appear in the final moment of the film, reprising their roles of Haymitch Abernathy, Katniss Everdeen and Peeta Mellark, respectively, from The Hunger Games (2012), The Hunger Games: Catching Fire (2013), The Hunger Games: Mockingjay - Part 1 (2014) and The Hunger Games: Mockingjay &#x2013; Part 2 (2015). blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

It was known that Lawrence and Hutcherson would return for the second prequel film. Harrelson could have been a given once they were confirmed, since his character centers the latest movie. In The Ballad of Songbirds and Snakes , which tells the villain origin story of Coriolanus Snow (Tom Blyth), Donald Sutherland&#x2019;s voice was used in the end to tie the first prequel film to the original four, in which Sutherland portrayed the poisonous president. Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

The Sunrise scene in particular is meaningful with these three actors behind their roles because it connects the past and present, bridging the gap between The Sunrise on the Reaping and Suzanne Collins&#x2019; original trilogy of books plus their film adaptations. Haymitch, in his Quarter Quell Hunger Games, did so much to advance the rebellion that would eventually bring down Panem, the Capitol and the barbaric tradition that killed children ever year. It was Katniss who ultimately gained the momentum from this spark &#x2014; symbolized by Haymitch&#x2019;s flint striker and more &#x2014; to topple the dystopian society and cruel reign of President Snow (Ralph Fiennes in Sunrise on the Reaping and Donald Sutherland in the first four films).

Katniss and Peeta wish Haymitch a happy birthday in the ending scene, symbolizing that he did, in fact, reach a birthday where the sun didn&#x2019;t rise on another reaping ceremony, which was his love Lenore Dove&#x2019;s (Whitney Peak) dying wish. It took another 25 years after his games, which doubled the amount of tributes entered as is custom for a Quarter Quell, to overcome the tyranny. The 50th Hunger Games added a wrinkle, or extra rule, to make those games extra gruesome. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

By then, Peeta and Katniss, who had already somewhat thwarted the Gamemakers by threatening to each eat poisonous nightlock berries and die for there to be no victor in their 74 th games, experienced a terrible Quarter Quell of their own. The 75 th Hunger Games &#x2014; or third Quarter Quell &#x2014; involved the wrinkle that each pair of district tributes would be reaped from their existing pool of victors.

The Catching Fire film made it seem like Plutarch Heavensbee (Philip Seymour Hoffman) and President Snow (Donald Sutherland) devised that wrinkle themselves to particularly torture Katniss and send her a message about her sedition. In the books, the founders of Panem left a box behind that laid out the rules of each Quarter Quell game, making it seem more like coincidence that this happened when a full-blown rebellion was close at hand.

While preparing for the third Quarter Quell, Katniss and Peeta leaned on Haymitch for his experience in the games in addition to meeting other victors turned mentors turned tributes once more like Mags (Lynn Cohen), Beetee (Jeffrey Wright), Wiress (Amanda Plummer) and others, younger versions of whom played roles in Haymitch&#x2019;s story before the big Catching Fire revolt as well.

&#x201C;The seeds of Haymitch Abernathy&#x2019;s backstory were planted over twenty years ago when I began the original trilogy,&#x201D; author Suzanne Collins wrote in a letter timed to the film&#x2019;s release . &#x201C;In Catching Fire , Katniss and Peeta watch the recap of his Second Quarter Quell games as he silently observes from the shadows. The Capitol had warped the true account and spun reality into vicious propaganda. For Haymitch to tell the truth about what happened would&#x2019;ve been too dangerous for his tributes and too traumatic for him.&#x201D;

At the end of the snippet, Haymitch goes to the meadow to feed his flock of geese, which he raises in memory of Lenore Dove, but not before Katniss and Peeta thank him, and he in return thanks them for their teamwork in dismantling the dictatorship they lived under for so long.

As for whether there could be more films in the franchise, it seems like it would come down to Collins and her decision to write another book or two. Fans have been particularly vocal about wanting more of one Finnick Odair&#x2019;s first Hunger Games, and director Francis Lawrence as well as star Joseph Zada have expressed interest in diving into Plutarch&#x2019;s (Jesse Plemons) story as well as the lore behind the mysterious District 13, which makes itself known in the Mockingjay books and films. Collins is known for writing these books only when she has something to say and express through them. The final scene at the end of Sunrise on the Reaping could make a great close to the story as is.

Let the grand con begin… Netflix has ordered a second season of Tokyo Swindlers , the Japanese crime thriller that turned Tokyo&#x2019;s high-stakes real estate market into one of the streamer&#x2019;s biggest local hits of 2024.

Go Ayano and Etsushi Toyokawa will reprise their roles as Takumi Tsujimoto and Harrison Yamanaka, respectively, with Hitoshi One returning as writer and director. Kohei Ninomiya, who previously directed episodes of the Japanese newsroom drama Elpis , will also write and direct. The new season is set to debut globally in 2027. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Movies "I'm in Preparation for the End of Our World": Golshifteh Farahani on Art, War and Her Tallinn Premiere Movies IDFA: 'The Year of the Ghost' and 'Memories of Lightning' Win Amsterdam Doc Fest Awards

Adapted from a novel by Japanese author Ko Shinjo, the first season follows Takumi, a negotiator recruited into Harrison&#x2019;s gang of real estate fraudsters. Their most ambitious scheme involves a property worth 10 billion yen (about $63 million), with the group maneuvering around developers and evading police as Takumi&#x2019;s troubled past and Harrison&#x2019;s ruthless methods gradually emerge.

The series topped Netflix&#x2019;s weekly series chart in Japan for six consecutive weeks &#x2014; a first since the rankings began &#x2014; and remained in the country&#x2019;s top 10 for 22 weeks overall, according to Netflix. It also appeared on the streamer&#x2019;s global non-English-language series chart for five consecutive weeks and reached the top 10 in 15 countries.

The show's success has also extended into Japanese popular culture, with dialogue and characters becoming memes on social media.

&#x201C;Right after it started streaming, Netflix came to me and said, &#x2018;Let&#x2019;s do Season 2!&#x2019;&#x201D; One said in a statement. &#x201C;I was terrified, thinking, &#x2018;There&#x2019;s no way we can top something that good&#x2026;&#x2019; But as I worked on the scripts, I started to think, &#x2018;Wait&#x2026; isn&#x2019;t this even better than Season 1?&#x2019; And that gradually turned into conviction.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Shinjo hinted that the returning con artists would be pursuing another formidable target. &#x201C;Human desire knows no limits,&#x201D; the author said. &#x201C;Searching for something beyond money alone, they will aim for an even bigger, even harder con.&#x201D;

Toyokawa offered a humorously ominous assessment of his task of stepping back into Harrison&#x2019;s shoes.

&#x201C;I have been reunited with a terrifying man,&#x201D; he said. &#x201C;He destroys my conscience, my sense of social decency, my love for my family. He destroys my life, my very humanity. I pray filming wraps before he consumes me. Imagine it: Harrison Yamanaka is always there in the mirror.&#x201D;

It looks like Billy Evans will get paid for the success of You Can See Everything after all. He just won't keep the money. Evans and his representatives have negotiated for the backend share he gave up to be paid out, according to two sources not affiliated with him or his partner Elizabeth Holmes. The money will go to an unnamed children's charity instead of to Evans, the sources said. While the exact percentage is unknown, the total payout will be a lot bigger now than it would have been even a few weeks ago. The film has grossed $89 million domestically to date, a jaw-dropping sum for a documentary. Subject-payment is a key plot point in Nathan Fielder and Lance Oppenheim's hit about the convicted Theranos founder and her life partner Evans. The film shows Evans back in 2023 seeking money from A24 without Holmes' knowledge, casting him in a greedy light; the filmmakers reluctantly then agree to pay him in order to secure access and make a deal. But a title card at the end says that "Billy Evans ultimately relinquished his negotiated share of the film's profits and would not receive backend compensation." Related Stories Movies IDA Documentary Awards Nominations: 'Concrete Land,' 'To Hold a Mountain,' 'You Can See Everything' Among Top Nominees Movies Billy Evans Fires Back at Amanda Seyfried and Nathan Fielder: "It's My Life and I Love It"

It is unclear if Evans at the time of that relinquishing secured a payout to charity with the title card omitting that point, or if Evans had fully given up on the possibility at the time and had a change of heart after the film was released and started raking in cash. Supporting the latter timing, Page Six reported on Oct. 23, a week after the movie opened, that Evans had contacted lawyers to try to restore his deal, with no word in that story that he had even succeeded in retaining counsel let alone striking a deal.

A representative for Evans did not provide comment. A spokesperson for A24 did not immediately reply to a request for comment. Documentary subjects these days often ask to be paid, and distributors sometimes agree, usually without giving up control of a film's final cut. That is what happened here until Evans decided to relinquish what he'd negotiated. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Speaking to The Hollywood Reporter this week, Evans said he made that decision "maybe five months ago" because the filmmakers "said it would help the project"

"I am totally stubborn, but if there's anything that I can do to help Liz regardless of the cost, I will do it,&#x201D; he said. (He explained his earlier push for money this way: "I'm a single dad with two kids whose best friend's about to be sent to prison. And at that time I didn't have a job. I'm trying to provide for my family and I'm really scared about what's to come." Evans is a member of the family that owns Evans Hotels, which operates three high-end Southern California properties including The Lodge at Torrey Pines, the Bahia Resort Hotel and the Catamaran Resort Hotel.) The new deal means A24 will be cutting a profit-participation check for Evans' role, just not to the entrepreneur himself. The move could still possibly help Evans' image. The entrepreneur has become a pop-culture villain thanks to moments like a domineering scene in which he shows Holmes how to whisk eggs, along with diatribes at filmmakers over questions he doesn't like. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Amanda Seyfried, who plays Holmes in the film's reconstructions, challenges Evans on camera and tells Fielder she wants to break up the couple. Fan boards, meanwhile, routinely debate his level of villainy.

Philippines actress Jorrybell Agoto, the star of Rafael Manuel&#x2019;s award-winning debut feature Filipi&#xF1;ana , has died aged 32.

Her family announced that she passed away on Tuesday, November 17, following a battle with lymphoma. Epicmedia Productions, the Philippine production company behind Filipi&#xF1;ana , posted on its Instagram account: &#x201C;We love you, Belle. No more pain.&#x201D;

Manuel posted: &#x201C;The tragedy of this loss cannot be put into words. The world has just lost one of its brightest stars. We have just lost a great friend. But our thoughts and prayers go out especially to Jorrybell&#x2019;s family who have just lost a loving older sister and a devoted daughter.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories News 'Buddy' Busts Out, Scares Up No. 6 Spot, Sets Record For Roadside Attractions, Saban - Specialty Box Office News Dark Comedy 'Buddy', Thriller 'Colony', John Boorman Doc Hit Theaters - Specialty Preview

Filipi&#xF1;ana premiered at this year&#x2019;s Sundance Film Festival where it won the Special Jury Award for Creative Vision in the World Cinema Dramatic Competition. It is also the Philippines&#x2019; entry for the Best International Feature category of next year&#x2019;s Oscars. Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

